Formalization of the D₅ dihedral group action on the mod 5 ray decomposition of natural numbers.

Key results proven:
1. `D5Structure.mod5_rays_are_D5_orbits`: The action of D₅ on the rays is formally equivariant with the action on ZMod 5 indices, confirming the structural link.
2. `D5Structure.spiral_respects_D5_rotation`: The logarithmic spiral embedding respects the rotational part of the D₅ action.
3. `D5Structure.pentagonal_mirror_is_reflection`: The pentagonal mirror operation corresponds to the reflection element in D₅.
4. `D5Structure.phi_from_pentagon_diagonal`: The golden ratio φ is derived from the geometry of the pentagon and is preserved under rotations.

Disproofs:
The conjectures that the "Pentagon rays" (1, 4) and "Pentagram rays" (2, 3) are invariant subsets under the full D₅ action were disproven (`D5Structure.pentagon_rays_not_D5_invariant` and `D5Structure.pentagram_rays_not_D5_invariant_proven`). While they are invariant under the reflection `sr 0` (pentagonal mirror), they are not invariant under general rotations or other reflections, as the action is transitive on the set of rays.
